[Section: 4. Game loop > Weaknesses]

- busy loop with no sleep/yield;

- no catch-up cap;

- no graceful thread termination;

- update and Swing repaint concurrency is unsynchronized;

- no pause/lifecycle model.

[Section: 9. OOP design > Weaknesses]

- deep getter chains from listeners;

- static/global constants;

- no generic entity/component model;

- no scene or level architecture;

- mutable booleans for many state flags.

[Section: 12. Resource handling > Weaknesses]

- null resource is not checked;

- `ImageIO.read()` can fail in ways not cleanly surfaced;

- try-with-resources would be cleaner.

[Section: 36. Product failure potential]

In a local prototype, failure cost is low. Principal technical failure modes are:

- missing sprite resource causing startup/runtime failure;

- thread lifecycle problems;

- high CPU usage from busy loop;

- animation state inconsistencies;

- no collision/physics despite platformer framing;

- platform/build ambiguity.

For a public game, lack of testing, accessibility and packaging would become significant quality barriers.

